# Duet firmware files that a separately published build replaces.
#
# One line per file:
#
#   <file> sha256:<checksum of the published build> <https location>
#
# The file has to be one the reprapfirmware package delivers below
# /opt/dsf/sd/firmware, because that is the name RepRapFirmware derives from
# the board type when it flashes; a build under any other name is never used.
# Only a published build is taken, checked against the pin: no local path, no
# fallback, a mismatch stops the build. See "Replacing a Duet firmware file"
# in the README, in particular why the build needs a version string of its
# own before any board is flashed with it.
#
# Example:
#   Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin sha256:0123...cdef https://github.com/Meltingplot/RepRapFirmware/releases/download/v3.7.0-rc.1+mp1/Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin
Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin sha256:9ee7b514f5b7e06e5015522bc69e7f7b57eb0be8368b3f72129ad3a38be87d25 https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.2%2B1-mp.2/Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin
Duet3Firmware_EXP1HCL.bin sha256:8f2a0981b93594f4ce5d5093f53cc750e424814a09522a0b087b0301d272985a https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.2%2B1-mp.2/Duet3Firmware_EXP1HCL.bin
Duet3Firmware_SZP.bin sha256:d3dc8eb789928353a8316ec28f1da0b1bd6ccb71c7f76b39170bfb90c6f4326e https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.2%2B1-mp.2/Duet3Firmware_SZP.bin
# Mainboard: RepRapFirmware 3.7-dev at upstream 3.7.0 (c83e79926), built by us
# against the Meltingplot library forks with a version string of its own, so
# DuetControlServer flashes it on an image update. The firmware reports its
# accelerometers under sensors.accelerometers, where DuetSoftwareFramework
# 3.7.0-rc.2 and later look for them; 3.7.0-rc.1 does not. Upstream 3.7.0
# loads the MB6HC's IAP image at 0x20458000 again, where the packaged
# Duet3_SBCiap32_MB6HC.bin is linked, and carries our fixes for macro and file
# requests over the SBC. Our CoreN2G discards the instructions the SAME70
# fetches from flash while reading the user signature, which made an MB6HC on
# 3.7.0-rc.2+1-mp.3 hard-fault in M122. On top of upstream, mp.2 lets the main
# task carry out G-code requests from other tasks, and does an emergency stop
# when an established SBC connection is lost, so the mainboard resets
# whenever DuetControlServer restarts or the Pi reboots and runs config.g
# again once it reconnects.
Duet3Firmware_MB6HC.bin sha256:fade0fb32603cdd083dd716afbc55c87506b8eaa71042e3c0b0850e32b0b6f6f https://github.com/Meltingplot/RepRapFirmware/releases/download/3.7.0-mp.2/Duet3Firmware_MB6HC.bin
